The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>
err = gssx_dec_name(xdr, &ctx->src_name);
if (err)
    return err;  // Leaks ctx->exported_context_token, ctx->state, ctx->mech
</text>
<text>
err = gssx_dec_name(xdr, &ctx->targ_name);
if (err)
    return err;  // Leaks ctx->exported_context_token, ctx->state, ctx->mech, ctx->src_name
</text>
<text>
if (unlikely(p == NULL))
    return -ENOSPC;  // Leaks status->mech (allocated earlier)
</text>
Reason:
In functions `gssx_dec_ctx`, `gssx_dec_status`, and `gssx_dec_name`, memory is allocated by `gssx_dec_buffer()` (via `kmemdup`) for buffer fields. When a subsequent decode operation fails, the functions immediately return an error code without freeing previously allocated buffers, causing memory leaks. For example, in `gssx_dec_ctx`, if `gssx_dec_name` for `src_name` succeeds but `gssx_dec_name` for `targ_name` fails, the memory allocated for `exported_context_token`, `state`, `mech`, and `src_name.display_name` becomes unreferenced and leaks. The early returns bypass cleanup of those allocations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>
if (err)
    goto out_free_src_name;  // Jump to cleanup for src_name and prior allocations
</text>
<text>
out_free_src_name:
    kfree(ctx->src_name.display_name.data);
    ctx->src_name.display_name.data = NULL;
</text>
<text>
out_free_mech:
    kfree(status->mech.data);
    status->mech.data = NULL;
    return err;
</text>
Reason:
The patch replaces direct `return err` statements with `goto out_free_*` labels that lead to cleanup code. For each function, specific labels free the buffers allocated for fields that were successfully decoded before the failure point. After freeing, the pointers are set to NULL to prevent double-free, and then the error is returned. This ensures that no memory is leaked when an XDR decoding error occurs mid-function. For example, in `gssx_dec_ctx`, if `gssx_dec_name` for `targ_name` fails, `out_free_targ_name` frees only `targ_name.display_name`, and fall-through labels (`out_free_src_name`, `out_free_mech`, etc.) free earlier allocations in reverse order. The same pattern is applied to `gssx_dec_status` and `gssx_dec_name`.

